  "sensory_adapter": "Fixed nearest-template parsing of normalized 8x8 pixels. Templates are deduplicated unlabeled base training patches ordered by pixel hash and independently permuted by role. Every Cartesian template pair gets an identically sized disjoint KC group, stratified by anatomical strength without labels. A single pair drives16 KCs; each of two pairs drives8 (4/hemisphere). Recognition and equal row pooling are engineered; pair valence is learned only in KC-to-MBON synapses. No equality branch, membership flag, labels or trained decision head in encoding.",
  "teaching": "Supervised valence via DAN pulses, not chosen-action correctness. Cue500ms freezes weights but accumulates traces; cue-offDAN200ms learns;250ms passive consolidation.",
  "decoder": {
    "score": "meanMBON11Hz-meanMBON07Hz-offset",
    "offset_hz": 0.0,
    "threshold_hz": 2.0,
    "calibration": "Global unlabeled training-image offset and deadband. No per-image output correction."
  },
